    <div class="container container-tight hero-inner section">
        <div class="row g-5 align-items-center">
            <div class="col-lg-6">
                <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--onink mb-3">
                    <span class="brand-mark" style="color:#f0a894"><svg width="16" height="16"><use href="#crawdad" /></svg></span>
                    Declarative browser automation · bring your own browser
                </span>
                <h1 class="display-hero mt-2 mb-3">Browser automations that <span class="accent">don't silently rot.</span></h1>
                <p class="lead-tight mb-4" style="max-width:36rem;">
                    Every automation versioned, watched, and replayable — on your browsers, into your storage, under your
                    keys. Ship a <strong style="color:#fff;font-weight:650">JSON payload</strong> instead of a Playwright
                    codebase, and never operate scraping infrastructure again.
                </p>
                <div class="d-flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-4">
                    <a class="btn btn-brand btn-lg px-4" href="/login">Start free</a>
                    <a class="btn btn-ghost-ink btn-lg px-4" href="#how">Read the docs</a>
                </div>
                <div class="trust-row d-flex flex-wrap align-items-center gap-2">
                    <span>Free tier — 2 concurrent runs</span>
                    <span class="dot">•</span>
                    <span>No credit card</span>
                    <span class="dot">•</span>
                    <span>BYO browser at every tier</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            @* proof: real payload + live trace *@
            <div class="col-lg-6">
                <div class="editor">
                    <div class="editor__bar">
                        <span class="editor__dot"></span><span class="editor__dot"></span><span class="editor__dot"></span>
                        <span class="editor__name">example.title.json</span>
                        <span class="editor__tag">POST /runs</span>
                    </div>
<pre class="code"><span class="p">{</span>
  <span class="k">"crawldad"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="s">"1"</span><span class="p">,</span>
  <span class="k">"name"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="s">"example.title"</span><span class="p">,</span>
  <span class="k">"inputs"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="p">{</span> <span class="k">"backend"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="p">{</span> <span class="k">"type"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="s">"backend"</span><span class="p">,</span> <span class="k">"required"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="n">true</span> <span class="p">}</span> <span class="p">},</span>
  <span class="k">"config"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="p">{</span> <span class="k">"backend"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="s">"input.backend"</span> <span class="p">},</span>
  <span class="k">"steps"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="p">[</span>
    <span class="p">{</span> <span class="k">"goto"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="p">{</span> <span class="k">"url"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="s">"https://example.com"</span> <span class="p">}</span> <span class="p">},</span>
    <span class="p">{</span> <span class="k">"waitForLoadState"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="p">{</span> <span class="k">"state"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="s">"load"</span> <span class="p">}</span> <span class="p">},</span>
    <span class="p">{</span> <span class="k">"set"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="p">{</span>
        <span class="k">"var"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="s">"title"</span><span class="p">,</span>
        <span class="k">"value"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="s">"trim(coalesce(text('h1'), ''))"</span>
    <span class="p">}</span> <span class="p">}</span>
  <span class="p">],</span>
  <span class="k">"result"</span><span class="p">:</span> <span class="s">"{ title: title }"</span>
<span class="p">}</span></pre>
                    <div style="border-top:1px solid var(--code-line)">
                        <div class="trace">
                            <div class="trace__row"><span class="tdot tdot--brand"></span><span class="trace__ev">StepStarted</span><span class="trace__data">{"index":0,"kind":"goto"}</span></div>
                            <div class="trace__row"><span class="tdot tdot--water"></span><span class="trace__ev">Navigated</span><span class="trace__data">{"url":"https://example.com"}</span></div>
                            <div class="trace__row"><span class="tdot tdot--ok"></span><span class="trace__ev">Extracted</span><span class="trace__data">{"var":"title"}</span></div>
                            <div class="trace__row"><span class="tdot tdot--ok"></span><span class="trace__ev" style="color:#7fe0b6;font-weight:600">RunSucceeded</span><span class="trace__data">stats: 812ms · 37 steps</span></div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="result-chip"><span class="tdot tdot--ok"></span><span><span style="color:#8fb6ff">"result"</span>: { <span style="color:#8fb6ff">"title"</span>: <span style="color:#7fe0b6">"Example Domain"</span> }</span></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <p class="text-center mt-2 mb-0" style="color:var(--ink-muted);font-size:.82rem;">
                    The proof is in the product — you watch <em>your own</em> browser session driven live over SSE.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

@* ================= HOW IT WORKS ================= *@
<section class="section" id="how">
    <div class="container container-tight">
        <div class="text-center mb-5">
            <div class="section-kicker mb-2">How it works</div>
            <h2 class="h2-section mb-2">Point at your browser. Declare the payload. Watch it run.</h2>
            <p class="lead-tight mx-auto" style="max-width:40rem;">Crawldad always dials <em>out</em> to a CDP endpoint, so your only question is "can our egress reach your browser?" No new infra, no VPN — first run in minutes.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row g-4">
            <div class="col-md-4">
                <div class="card-soft card-hover p-4 h-100">
                    <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-3 mb-3"><span class="step-num">1</span><span class="persona-tag" style="color:var(--water)">Connect</span></div>
                    <h3 class="h4 mb-2">Point at your browser</h3>
                    <p class="mb-0" style="color:var(--muted)">Register a <span class="kbd-mono">connectUrl</span> for Browserbase, Browserless, a self-hosted CDP edge, or a local-Chrome tunnel. The browser stays <em>your</em> account — Crawldad never resells compute.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-4">
                <div class="card-soft card-hover p-4 h-100">
                    <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-3 mb-3"><span class="step-num">2</span><span class="persona-tag" style="color:var(--water)">Declare</span></div>
                    <h3 class="h4 mb-2">Declare the payload</h3>
                    <p class="mb-0" style="color:var(--muted)">A payload is one JSON program — <span class="kbd-mono">goto</span>, <span class="kbd-mono">click</span>, <span class="kbd-mono">fill</span>, extract — with real loops and content-aware conditions. No <span class="kbd-mono">eval</span>, an inspectable effect surface.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-4">
                <div class="card-soft card-hover p-4 h-100">
                    <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-3 mb-3"><span class="step-num">3</span><span class="persona-tag" style="color:var(--water)">Observe</span></div>
                    <h3 class="h4 mb-2">Watch it run live</h3>
                    <p class="mb-0" style="color:var(--muted)">Stream the trace over SSE, replay the exact pinned revision, and open the failure screenshot. When a selector drifts, the run tells you — not your customer.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<hr class="hr-fade container container-tight">

@* ================= PERSONAS / ON-RAMPS ================= *@
<section class="section" id="personas">
    <div class="container container-tight">
        <div class="text-center mb-5">
            <div class="section-kicker mb-2">Three on-ramps</div>
            <h2 class="h2-section mb-2">One topology fact, three ways in</h2>
            <p class="lead-tight mx-auto" style="max-width:42rem;">Because Crawldad reaches your browser (never the other way around), the same product fits a laptop, a team, or a data center — and the slot ladder maps onto them exactly.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row g-4">
            <div class="col-lg-4">
                <div class="card-soft p-4 h-100 d-flex flex-column">
                    <span class="pill mb-3" style="align-self:flex-start;background:var(--brand-tint);border-color:var(--brand-line);color:var(--brand-strong)">Solo dev → your machine</span>
                    <h3 class="h4 mb-2">A tunnel you already know</h3>
                    <p style="color:var(--muted)">Expose local Chrome's debugging port through <span class="kbd-mono">ngrok</span> or <span class="kbd-mono">cloudflared</span> and pass the <span class="kbd-mono">wss://</span> URL as a credential reference. Zero novelty — the same motion you use to receive webhooks locally.</p>
                    <div class="mt-auto pt-2" style="color:var(--water);font-weight:600;font-size:.9rem">Free tier · 2 slots · the whole front door</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-4">
                <div class="card-soft p-4 h-100 d-flex flex-column" style="border-color:var(--brand-line)">
                    <span class="pill mb-3" style="align-self:flex-start;background:var(--brand-tint);border-color:var(--brand-line);color:var(--brand-strong)">Mid team → Browserbase / Browserless</span>
                    <h3 class="h4 mb-2">The designed happy path</h3>
                    <p style="color:var(--muted)">Trivial to connect, nothing to build. This is where collaboration and continuity begin to matter: a shared payload registry, revision review, longer retention, and webhooks into your stack.</p>
                    <div class="mt-auto pt-2" style="color:var(--water);font-weight:600;font-size:.9rem">Team & Scale · 10–50+ slots</div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-4">
                <div class="card-soft p-4 h-100 d-flex flex-column">
                    <span class="pill mb-3" style="align-self:flex-start;background:var(--brand-tint);border-color:var(--brand-line);color:var(--brand-strong)">Crawling farm → your data centers</span>
                    <h3 class="h4 mb-2">Your perimeter, our plane</h3>
                    <p style="color:var(--muted)">Expose a TLS-terminated CDP edge and allowlist Crawldad's stable egress IPs. Where volume lives: the slot curve bends down, with dedicated egress, SSO/SLA, and a single-tenant instance inside your perimeter.</p>
                    <div class="mt-auto pt-2" style="color:var(--water);font-weight:600;font-size:.9rem">Scale & Enterprise · hundreds of slots</div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

@* ================= FEATURES ================= *@
<section class="section" id="features" style="background:var(--surface-2);border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);">
    <div class="container container-tight">
        <div class="text-center mb-5">
            <div class="section-kicker mb-2">What you actually get</div>
            <h2 class="h2-section mb-2">The reliability layer, not the electrons</h2>
            <p class="lead-tight mx-auto" style="max-width:42rem;">We price the interpreter, the retry taxonomy, the checkpoint saga, and the drift tooling that would otherwise rot on your shelf. Every capability in the grid below is live in the product today.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="row g-4">
            @* 1 *@
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
                <div class="card-soft p-4 h-100">
                    <span class="feat-ico mb-3"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M8 9l3 3l-3 3" /><path d="M14 15h3" /><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2" /></svg></span>
                    <h3 class="h5 mb-2">Declarative JSON payloads</h3>
                    <p class="mb-0" style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.93rem">Real loops with mandatory safety caps, content-aware conditions, and a composable document that's diffable, storable, and LLM-generatable — no <span class="kbd-mono">eval</span>, ever.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            @* 2 *@
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
                <div class="card-soft p-4 h-100">
                    <span class="feat-ico mb-3"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 12a9 9 0 1 0 9-9" /><path d="M3 4v4h4" /><path d="M12 8v4l3 2" /></svg></span>
                    <h3 class="h5 mb-2">Live SSE trace</h3>
                    <p class="mb-0" style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.93rem">Watch your own browser driven live, step by step. Reconnect with <span class="kbd-mono">Last-Event-ID</span> and resume exactly where you left off — the durable stream loses no frame.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            @* 3 *@
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
                <div class="card-soft p-4 h-100">
                    <span class="feat-ico mb-3"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M15 4v4H9V4" /><path d="M4 8h16v10a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z" /><path d="M12 12v4" /><path d="M10 14h4" /></svg></span>
                    <h3 class="h5 mb-2">Replay pinned revisions</h3>
                    <p class="mb-0" style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.93rem">Re-execute the exact revision plus script hash the original run recorded — the script is guaranteed identical. That guarantee is the whole basis of the drift story.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            @* 4 *@
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
                <div class="card-soft p-4 h-100">
                    <span class="feat-ico mb-3"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2" /><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3" /><path d="M7 8h.01" /></svg></span>
                    <h3 class="h5 mb-2">Failure screenshots + capture</h3>
                    <p class="mb-0" style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.93rem">A step fails and you get the PNG of the failing page — and, with <span class="kbd-mono">captureOnFailure</span>, its full HTML banked to <em>your</em> storage. The clearest possible drift diagnostic.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            @* 5 *@
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
                <div class="card-soft p-4 h-100">
                    <span class="feat-ico mb-3"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 17l4-6 4 3 4-7 4 5" /><path d="M3 21h18" /><path d="M3 4v13" /></svg></span>
                    <h3 class="h5 mb-2">Drift monitoring</h3>
                    <p class="mb-0" style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.93rem">A baseline/delta signal — not a naive miss count — flags a selector that matched at baseline but is newly gone. Query a payload's drift status on demand — per-revision baseline, tunable threshold — and read each run's pinned-vs-head revision drift alongside it.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            @* 6 *@
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
                <div class="card-soft p-4 h-100">
                    <span class="feat-ico mb-3"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M13 3l-1 9h6l-7 9 1-9H6z" /></svg></span>
                    <h3 class="h5 mb-2">Signed webhooks</h3>
                    <p class="mb-0" style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.93rem">Get pushed a run's terminal disposition — HMAC-signed, ref-only, at-least-once with backoff retry on an independent channel. A slow receiver never affects a run.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            @* 7 *@
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
                <div class="card-soft p-4 h-100">
                    <span class="feat-ico mb-3"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 5H7a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v12a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h10a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V7a2 2 0 0 0-2-2h-2" /><rect x="9" y="3" width="6" height="4" rx="1" /><path d="M9 14l2 2 4-4" /></svg></span>
                    <h3 class="h5 mb-2">Fixtures & CI regression</h3>
                    <p class="mb-0" style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.93rem">Record a live session once, then replay any revision against it — deterministically, zero live traffic — so CI golden-gates a payload before it ever touches the real site.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            @* 8 *@
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
                <div class="card-soft p-4 h-100">
                    <span class="feat-ico mb-3"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 7c0-1.7 3.6-3 8-3s8 1.3 8 3-3.6 3-8 3-8-1.3-8-3z" /><path d="M4 7v10c0 1.7 3.6 3 8 3s8-1.3 8-3V7" /><path d="M4 12c0 1.7 3.6 3 8 3s8-1.3 8-3" /></svg></span>
                    <h3 class="h5 mb-2">Retention & right-to-erasure</h3>
                    <p class="mb-0" style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.93rem">Per-tier timeline windows, with a one-call <span class="kbd-mono">DELETE</span> that hard-erases a run's result, timeline, and event stream in a single tenant-scoped transaction.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            @* 9 *@
            <div class="col-md-6 col-lg-4">
                <div class="card-soft p-4 h-100">
                    <span class="feat-ico mb-3"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M12 3l7 3v5c0 4.5-3 8-7 10-4-2-7-5.5-7-10V6z" /><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4" /></svg></span>
                    <h3 class="h5 mb-2">BYO browser, storage & keys</h3>
                    <p class="mb-0" style="color:var(--muted);font-size:.93rem">Table stakes at every tier including free — never an upsell. Secrets are vault references typed straight into the field; they never enter an expression, a variable, or the trace.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

